WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.568
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.406
Here in the U.S.,
the Paris attackers

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.475
touched off a ferocious debate
about Syrian refugees.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.979
You might remember,
President Obama had pledged
to accept at least 10,000

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:17.082
over the next year but after
news broke that one of the
attackers may have posed

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:20.786
as a refugee and
entered Europe through Greece
with a fake Syrian passport,

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.255
many U.S. officials had
second thoughts.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.725
REPORTER:<i> Thirty-one
 governors now oppose,</i>

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:30.930
<i> are refusing or suspending
 the resettlement of Syrian
 refugees into their states.</i>

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:36.202
Okay, that's pretty extreme but
it's also pretty meaningless
for two reasons.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.972
One, governors don't have the
legal authority to ban refugees.

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:46.045
And two, even if they could,
Syrians can't just walk between
states like anyone else.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:49.516
The lines on maps are not
crocodile-filled moats.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.117
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:55.087
Presidential candidates also
got involved with this
anti-refugee rhetoric.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.257
Donald Trump, Ben Carson
and Marco Rubio

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:00.593
called for halts
to all Syrian refugees
entering the country.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:06.866
And others like Ted Cruz and
Jeb Bush argued we could take
some if they were Christian.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:11.271
If you're wondering how
that would work,
let Jeb Bush explain.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:17.176 line:0%
What, you're a Christian,
I mean, you can prove
you're a Christian. It's--

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:20.480
-How?
-I think you can prove it.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:23.315
I think you can prove it,

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:25.451
I'm pretty sure
you can prove it.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:26.919
You see, I'll tell you how.
You see...

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:30.423
a Christian has ears that
protrude out from their heads,

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.726
whereas non-Christians lack
external ears all together.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:34.827
You know what? Hold on.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.896
I'm thinking about seals
and sea lions.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.800
I often get them confused...
Forget everything I said about
Christians and Muslims.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.703
I don't know
what I'm talking about.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.405
And it was not just Republicans.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.607
The Democratic mayor of
Roanoke, Virginia, David Bowers

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:51.210
was so terrified of Syrian
refugees, he used

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.614
the worst possible historical
example to prove his point.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.515 line:0%
REPORTER: Mayor
David Bowers wrote:

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.017 line:0%
(REPORTER READING LETTER)

00:02:10.662 --> 00:02:11.864
Wow!

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.533
Did he not realize that
Japanese internment camps

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.470
are one of this nation's
greatest sources of shame?

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.238
It's one of the parts of
FDR's legacy

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.674
his family would
most like you to forget.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.577 line:0%
And bear in mind, this is a man
who's own biopic featured

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.813 line:0%
featured a scene of him
getting a hand job

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.381 line:0%
from his distant cousin.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.918
♪ (ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.398
Did I have to show you that?
No.

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:49.535
Did I want to?
Absolutely, I did!

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:53.972
But this week's events actually
call to mind a chapter
from FDR's time in office

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:58.611
that is even more shameful
than the saddest and classiest
hand job of all time.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.980
Specifically, when in 1939,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.250
U.S. authorities turned away
a ship containing

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.687
more than 900 mostly Jewish
refugees from Germany.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.622
Something American newsrooms
at the time

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.724
tried to put a positive spin on.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.826
NARRATOR:<i> Nine hundred-seven
 Jewish unfortunates</i>

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:15.795
<i> without a country
 permitted to land</i>

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:19.231
<i> in Belgium after five weeks
 of suspense afloat.</i>

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:21.767
<i> Through American generosity,
 they will find at least</i>

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:24.637
<i> temporary shelter
in France, Holland and England.</i>

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:30.376
Yes. We sent a boat of Jews
back to Europe in 1939.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.745
More than a quarter of them
then died in the war.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.348
So this Thanksgiving, when
your grandmother's complaining

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:39.985
about your new piercing saying
your generation is terrible.
Simply reply, "Okay, Nanna."

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:43.556
"But at least we didn't send
Jews back to Europe in 1939."

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.024
Then break off a turkey leg,
drop it like a microphone

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.060
and you've just won the dinner.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.396
Dinner over!

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.065
Although...
let's be honest here.

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:57.403
Every generation has had
it's own ugly reaction
to refugees.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:01.240
Whether they are the Irish,
the Vietnamese, the Cubans
or the Haitians.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.109
And those fears have been
broadly unfounded.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:07.746
In fact, there was only one time
in American history when
the fear of refugees

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:10.550
wiping everyone out
did actually come true.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.786
And we'll all be sitting
around a table
celebrating it on Thursday.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:19.525
And look, it is absolutely fair.
It's fair to be concerned

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.693
about safety in the wake
of these attacks.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.996
And it's fair to wonder
who we're letting in

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.332
and what sort of
screening system is in place.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.535
Unfortunately, many
of the people talking about it
this week,

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:32.905
don't seem to have
the first idea
of what we're doing.

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:35.874 line:0%
Do we know who these people are?
No.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.310 line:0%
Are they properly vetted?
No.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:42.047 line:0%
How do you vet them?
There's no possible way
to vet them.

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:45.384 line:0%
There's virtually no vetting
'cause there are no databases
in Syria.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:46.852 line:0%
There are no government records.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.420 line:0%
We don't know
who these people are.

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:51.524
Look, it is difficult
to vet people coming out
of a war zone.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.926
But it's not like
we're just letting anyone in.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:58.063
We are the United States
of America, not Arizona State.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:01.033
Because for the...
Just for the record here.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:05.103
Let me walk you through
what our screening process
actually is.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.440
If you're a refugee, first,
you apply through

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.675
the United Nations'
High Commissioner for Refugees,

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.211
which collects documents and
performs interviews.

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:15.647
Incidentally, less than
one percent
of refugees worldwide

00:05:15.747 --> 00:05:17.350
end up being recommended
for resettlement.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.551
But, if you're one of them,
you might be referred

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:22.188
to the state department
to begin the vetting process.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.356
At this point, more information
is collected.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:26.525
You'll be put through
security screenings by the

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.160
National
Counterterrorism Center,

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.729
the FBI, and the
Department of Homeland Security.

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:33.899
And if you're a Syrian refugee,
you'll get an additional
layer of screening

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.601
called the Syria
in-house review,

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.102
which may include
a further check

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:39.138
by a special part of
Homeland Security,

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.474
the USCIS Fraud detection,
and National Security directors.

00:05:42.574 --> 00:05:45.745
And don't relax yet, 'cause
we've barely even started.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.447
Then, you finally get
an interview with USCIS officers

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:50.049
and you'll also be fingerprinted

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.318
so your prints can be run
through the biometric databases

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.453
of the FBI, the Department of
Homeland Security,

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:55.788
and the Department of Defense.

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:58.224
And if you make it through
all that, you'll then have
health screenings,

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.892
which, let's face it,
may not go too well for you,

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.495
'cause you may have
given yourself a stroke

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:04.363
getting through
this process so far.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.132
But if everything
comes back clear,

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.568
you'll be enrolled in
Cultural Orientation classes

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:11.137
all while your information
continues to be checked

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.638
recurrently against
terrorist databases

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.206
to makes sure that
no new information

00:06:14.306 --> 00:06:16.041
comes in
that wasn't caught before.

00:06:16.141 --> 00:06:19.412
All of that has to happen
before you get near a plane.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:23.349
This process typically takes
18-24 months
once you've been referred

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.518
by the U.N.
to the United States.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:29.054
This is the most rigorous
vetting anyone has to face

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:30.956
before entering this country.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:34.526
No terrorist in their right mind
would choose this path

00:06:34.626 --> 00:06:37.263
when the visa process
requires far less efforts.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:40.733
But nevertheless, the House
still voted on Thursday

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.902
to add a few more steps.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:47.640
<i> The house voted 289 to 137 for
 tougher screening procedures</i>

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.109
<i> requiring the FBI director</i>

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:53.479
<i> to sign off on each
 and every refugee.</i>

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:57.049
He signs off...
That is ridiculous!

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:59.685
At this point, why don't we just
include a pie-eating contest,

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:03.355
a spelling bee,
and an evening wear portion.

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:08.060
But the really hard truth here
is no one can promise

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.230
that someone dangerous still
might not slip through.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.232
And while that risk should
not be denied,

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:16.001
it also should
not be wildly inflated.

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:17.169 line:0%
Let me ask this.

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:19.472 line:0%
If you bought a five-pound
bag of peanuts,

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:22.041 line:0%
and you knew that
in the five-pound bag of peanuts

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:25.111 line:0%
there were about 10 peanuts
that were deadly poisonous,

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.445 line:0%
would you feed them
to your kids?

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:27.680 line:0%
The answer is no.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:30.349
Yeah, of course it's no.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.084
For starters, you should
give your kids and actual meal,

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.954
not a handful of peanuts
because they're human children

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.322
not circus elephants.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.990
But second,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.392
we wanted to do
the math on what he just said.

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:44.096
So we bought five pounds
of peanuts and we counted them.

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:46.264
There are about
1,000 nuts in there.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.799
So if 10 of them
are poisoned,

00:07:47.899 --> 00:07:49.469
Mike Huckabee
is essentially suggesting

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:53.038
that about one of every 100
refugees is a terrorist.

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:57.009 line:0%
But in reality, of the more than
784,000 refugees

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.211 line:0%
admitted to the U.S.
since 9/11,

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.748 line:0%
only three have
been arrested for
planning terrorist activities.

00:08:02.848 --> 00:08:05.584 line:0%
None of which, by the way,
resulted in attacks here.

00:08:05.684 --> 00:08:09.221 line:0%
So, the actual known ratio
of arrested terror suspects

00:08:09.321 --> 00:08:11.624
to refugees is not one in 100.

00:08:11.724 --> 00:08:14.994
It's one in roughly 261,000.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:17.897
Peanuts themselves
have killed far more people

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:21.934
in the last decade
than terrorist refugees.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:24.970
Oh, I'll go one step further!

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.073
Men named Mike have
killed more people

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:32.811
than terrorist refugees
and I don't see us
rounding all of them up.

00:08:32.911 --> 00:08:36.415
And that's kind of the point.
Because as reasonably adults,

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:39.618
we accept tiny amounts of risk
baked into our everyday lives.

00:08:39.718 --> 00:08:43.856
We drive cars, despite knowing
around 30,000 of us
die in them each year.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:48.594
We go swimming, despite the fact
10 people a day
die from drowning.

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:52.631 line:0%
Twenty Americans every year
are killed by cows.

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:56.602 line:0%
But no one is saying we should
expel all cows from the country.

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:59.404 line:0%
We're happy just taking them
out one at a time, thinking,

00:08:59.504 --> 00:09:03.108
"Well, we got them before
they got us."

00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:04.844
This is what freedom
tastes like.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:10.649
Any rational person knows
you cannot completely
eliminate risk.

00:09:10.749 --> 00:09:11.950
You can only manage it.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.186
And we do it with peanuts
and cars, and swimming,

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:17.222
and hamburgers,
and men named Mike.

00:09:17.322 --> 00:09:19.425
'Cause we rightly think that
they're worth the risk.

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.760
And I would argue for the
tremendous good we could do,

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.596
and the low-level
of risk involved,

00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:25.731
refugees are worth it, too.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.399
And you may disagree,

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:30.435
but it is worth noting
that as we devise new ways

00:09:30.535 --> 00:09:31.904
to close our doors this week,

00:09:32.004 --> 00:09:34.706
France, which has
just suffered a terror attack

00:09:34.807 --> 00:09:36.775
and has far less ability
to police its borders,

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:38.010
did this.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:39.812 line:0%
REPORTER:<i> French President
 Francoise Hollande says</i>

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:42.881 line:0%
<i> France will still welcome
 refugees into the country</i>

00:09:42.981 --> 00:09:44.616 line:0%
<i> despite the Paris massacre.</i>

00:09:44.716 --> 00:09:46.886 line:0%
<i> Speaking at a gathering of the
 nation's mayors,</i>

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:49.021 line:0%
<i> he said France
 will keep its commitment</i>

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:52.158 line:0%
<i> to take in 30,000 refugees
 over the next two years.</i>

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:55.761 line:0%
<i>Hollande added that France will
 remain a country of freedom.</i>

00:09:56.261 --> 00:09:59.731
Yeah, because they think it's
worth the risk!

00:09:59.831 --> 00:10:02.734
And it's frankly not ideal.
Francoise Hollande,

00:10:02.834 --> 00:10:05.337
a man who broke up with his
partner of 30 years,

00:10:05.437 --> 00:10:07.239
in order to shack up
with a lover

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:09.908
who looks exactly like her,
just 10 years younger

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:13.445
Only to quickly leave that lover
for another lover,

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.814
who looks
exactly like the second lover,

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:18.083
just 10 years younger again.

00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:21.420
That man is currently
functioning as an effective
moral compass

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.855
for your politicians.

